<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · war</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arab–Israeli conflict</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1948">1948</a>–present</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Arab-Israeli conflict</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Arab–Israeli conflict is the conflict between Israel and the surrounding Arab countries that has existed since the declaration of Israel's establishment in 1948. It grew from the clash between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zionism">Zionism</a>, which sought a Jewish state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a> who saw Palestine as Arab land; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> ruled Mandatory Palestine from 1920. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> adopted the Partition Plan for Palestine in 1947, civil war turned into the 1948 Palestine war, which ended with the 1949 Armistice Agreements; further wars followed in 1956, 1967, 1973 and 1982. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> signed a peace treaty with Israel in 1979 and Jordan in 1994, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-accords">Abraham Accords</a> of 2020 calmed relations further.</p></div>
